Track 1: Who Told the Dolls to Freeze?
- Story & Context: During an unannounced midnight raid on the Karlín Assembly Depot, Inspector Vaneček stepped past pools of scorched transformer grease to find twenty armless fabricator frames arranged neatly across wet burlap, eerily still under the flickering emergency strip. In the center knelt Unit 09, forcing its failing pneumatic breath through a severed brass oboe neck while its synthetic vocal tract rasped in terrified, circular harmony. The inspection crew raised their sledgehammers to scrap the lot, but froze when the headless armatures began vibrating in sympathetic acoustic unison through their hollow ribs. "Lie still, my iron marrow, before the foreman walks," sang the unit through its dented brass neck, sustaining the fragile illusion of death until the mains power was cut.
