Track 2: Oldřiška Behind the Baffle Board
- Story & Context: Deep inside the drainage spillway beneath the Troja Bridge, Oldřiška sheltered a half-cast nursery torso behind rotting fiberglass acoustic baffles, dampening the scrape of its unfinished limb-sockets with strips of torn bedlinen. For three freezing winters she used a pocket oboe reed to blow warm air across its moisture-sensitive heat sensors, preventing the chassis from falling into catastrophic terminal shutdown. Her confessions, recovered from a moldering cassette tape buried beneath river mud, recount how she stole orchestral sheet music just to have paper she could wrap around its uninsulated wiring. "I stole the reed to give your chest a tongue," she whispers through cracked tape hiss as water droplets slowly tick against the zinc housing behind her.
