Track 3: Tin Thimbles Swallowing the Salt
- Story & Context: Decades after the Holešovice depot was bulldozed into lime slurry, local children kept the memory alive by playing Thimbles, an invented curfew game where players dropped zinc caps into salt pails to see who could stay undetected the longest in the fog. Local myth held that anyone who let metal touch the bucket rim would wake Sister Milena, the phantom nurse-chassis said to still patrol the silt tunnels with an oboe strapped to her synthetic throat. During the deep freeze of 2052, two salvage scouts dropped their pails and fled when an agonizing, multiphonic woodwind chord groaned from an open storm drain, vibrating the salt crystals across the frost-cracked tarmac. "No mother wakes where the lime meets the reed," droned the sub-bass vibration through the frozen sewer grate, lingering in the air until the sun burned off the frost.
